  "question": {
    "text": "The intercept on the line \\(y=x\\) by the circle \\(x^2+y^2-2 x=0\\) is \\(A B\\). Equation of the circle with \\(A B\\) as diameter is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\\(x^2+y^2=1\\)",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\\(\\mathrm{x}(\\mathrm{x}-1)+\\mathrm{y}(\\mathrm{y}-1)=0\\)",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\\(x^2+y^2=2\\)",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\\((x-1)(x-2)+(y-1)+(y-2)=0\\)",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hints: \\(2 x^2-2 x=0 \\quad x(x+1)=0 \\quad x=0,1 ; y=0,1\\)\n\\((0,0),(1,1)\\) as diametric ends\n\\(\\begin{aligned}\n& (x-0)(x-1)+(y+0)(y-1)=0 \\\\\n& x^2+y^2-x-y=0\n\\end{aligned}\\)"
